body:
WP10 -> WP03: the CAVLC corruption has a concrete cause in n2avc_write_residual() (avc/n2avc_cavlc.c:119-128): run_before is coded in the wrong direction.

Current code:
    for (i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        int run = pos[i + 1] - pos[i] - 1;
        if (zeros_left > 0) {
            int zl = zeros_left > 6 ? 7 : zeros_left;
            n2avc_put_vlc(w, &n2avc_cw_run_before[run][zl]);
            zeros_left -= run;
        }
    }

Clause 9.2.3/9.2.4 codes run_before from the highest-frequency coefficient down: for i = TotalCoeff-1 down to 1, run = pos[i] - pos[i-1] - 1, zerosLeft starts at total_zeros and decreases. Your loop emits the same run values in the opposite order, so the decoder places the coefficients at different positions (and with zerosLeft out of step it can index a run/zerosLeft combination whose table entry is len 0, which sets w->overflow and forces the I_PCM fallback for every following MB -- that is the all-I_PCM 176x144 frame and, with n2bw_trailing spinning on overflow, the P-mode hang).

Why your worked-example unit test does not catch it: for coefficients at positions 1,3,4,5,7 the run list is [1,0,0,1] lowest-first and [1,0,0,1] highest-first -- palindromic. Use a non-palindromic block in the test, e.g. positions 0,1,4,5,9 (runs lowest-first [0,2,0,3], highest-first [3,0,2,0]).

Evidence (gdb on the -O2 CLI, 16x16 gradient, QP 26): at n2avc_cavlc.c:125 with i=0, n=5, run=0, zl=7, zeros_left=11; the first call is fine, a later one hits n2avc_put_vlc with c->len == 0 -> w->overflow=1. At -O0 the same input produces a 257-byte stream that ffmpeg rejects with "corrupted macroblock 0 0 (total_coeff=-1)"; its slice header parses correctly (first_mb 0, slice_type 7, frame_num 0, idr_pic_id 0, slice_qp_delta 0, disable_deblocking 1), so the fault is in the residual syntax, not the header.

Suggested fix:
    for (i = n - 1; i >= 1; i--) {
        int run = pos[i] - pos[i - 1] - 1;
        if (zeros_left > 0) {
            int zl = zeros_left > 6 ? 7 : zeros_left;
            n2avc_put_vlc(w, &n2avc_cw_run_before[run][zl]);
            zeros_left -= run;
        }
    }

The n2bw_trailing overflow spin is still a separate one-line fix (if (w->overflow) return;), otherwise a genuinely too-small slice buffer will hang instead of returning N2AVC_E_OVERFLOW.
